chr	EMBL	CDS	582401	583558	.	-	0	EC_number=2.1.1.-;codon_start=1;locus_tag=ACN6KE_000526;note=SplB-like protein%2C Radical SAM superfamily: Enzymes of this family generate radicals by combining a 4Fe-4S cluster and S-adenosylmethionine %28SAM%29 in close proximity. They are characterized by a conserved CxxxCxxC motif%2C which coordinates the conserved iron-sulfur cluster. Mechanistically%2C they share the transfer of a single electron from the iron-sulfur cluster to SAM%2C which leads to its reductive cleavage to methionine and a 5%27-deoxyadenosyl radical%2C which%2C in turn%2C abstracts a hydrogen from the appropriately positioned carbon atom. Depending on the enzyme%2C SAM is consumed during this process or it is restored and reused. Radical SAM enzymes catalyze steps in metabolism%2C DNA repair%2C the biosynthesis of vitamins and coenzymes%2C and the biosynthesis of many antibiotics.%2CHigh confidence in function and specificity;product=Radical SAM-domain containing protein;protein_id=ACN6KE:HE616890.530;transl_table=11;
