plasmid_a2	EMBL	CDS	12498	13889	.	-	0	EC_number=3.4.21.107;codon_start=1;db_xref=GO:0009266,GO:30288%2CGO,GO:4252%2CGO,GO:5886%2CGO,GO:6457%2CGO,GO:6515%2CGO,GO:6979%2CGO;function=DegP acts as a chaperone at low temperatures but switches to a peptidase %28heat shock protein%29 at higher temperatures. It degrades transiently denatured and unfolded proteins which accumulate in the periplasm following heat shock or other stress conditions. DegP is efficient with Val-Xaa and Ile- Xaa peptide bonds%2C suggesting a preference for beta-branched side chain amino acids. Only unfolded proteins devoid of disulfide bonds appear capable of being cleaved%2C thereby preventing non- specific proteolysis of folded proteins. Its proteolytic activity is essential for the survival of cells at elevated temperatures. It can degrade IciA%2C ada%2C casein%2C globin and PapA. DegP shares specificity with DegQ. DegP is also involved in the biogenesis of folded outer-membrane proteins %28OMP%29 %28By similarity%29.;locus_tag=ACN6KE_004776;note=High confidence in function and specificity;product=putative serine endoprotease;protein_id=ACN6KE:XXX.16;transl_table=11;
