plasmid_e	EMBL	CDS	1742816	1744486	.	-	0	EC_number=3.6.3.-;codon_start=1;db_xref=GO:0016887,GO:5524%2CGO;function=ATPase components of various ABC-type transport systems%2C contain duplicated ATPase;locus_tag=ACN6KE_006664;note=The ABC transporter subfamily specific for the transport of dipeptides%2C oligopeptides%2C and nickel %28NikDE%29. The NikABCDE system of E. coli belongs to this family and is composed of the periplasmic binding protein NikA%2C two integral membrane components %28NikB and NikC%29%2C and two ATPase %28NikD and NikE%29. The NikABCDE transporter is synthesized under anaerobic conditions to meet the increased demand for nickel resulting from hydrogenase synthesis. The molecular mechanism of nickel uptake in many bacteria and most archaea is not known. Many other members of this ABC family are also involved in the uptake of dipeptides and oligopeptides. The oligopeptide transport system %28Opp%29 is a five-component ABC transport composed of a membrane-anchored substrate binding proteins %28SRP%29%2C OppA%2C two transmembrane proteins%2C OppB and OppC%2C and two ATP-binding domains%2C OppD and OppF.%2CFamily membership;product=putative ATP-binding component of ABC transporter;protein_id=ACN6KE:HE616899.1642;transl_table=11;
plasmid_e	EMBL	CDS	1744498	1745625	.	-	0	codon_start=1;db_xref=GO:0016020,GO:5215%2CGO,GO:6810%2CGO;function=ABC-type dipeptide/oligopeptide/nickel transport systems%2C permease components;locus_tag=ACN6KE_006665;note=RecName: Full:Oligopeptide transport system permease Transmembrane subunit %28TM%29 found in Periplasmic Binding Protein %28PBP%29-dependent ATP-Binding Cassette %28ABC%29 transporters which generally bind type 2 PBPs. These types of transporters consist of a PBP%2C two TMs%2C and two cytoplasmic ABC ATPase subunits%2C and are mainly involved in importing solutes from the environment. The solute is captured by the PBP which delivers it to a gated translocation pathway formed by the two TMs. The two ABCs bind and hydrolyze ATP and drive the transport reaction. For these transporters the ABCs and TMs are on independent polypeptide chains. These systems transport a diverse range of substrates. Most are specific for a single substrate or a group of related substrates%3B however some transporters are more promiscuous%2C transporting structurally diverse substrates such as the histidine/lysine and arginine transporter in Enterobacteriaceae. In the latter case%2C this is achieved through binding different PBPs with different specificities to the TMs. For other promiscuous transporters such as the multiple-sugar transporter Msm of Streptococcus mutans%2C the PBP has a wide substrate specificity. These transporters include the maltose-maltodextrin%2C phosphate and sulfate transporters%2C among others.%2CFamily membership;product=putative permease component of ABC transporter;protein_id=ACN6KE:HE616899.1643;transl_table=11;
plasmid_e	EMBL	CDS	1745622	1746635	.	-	0	codon_start=1;db_xref=GO:0016020,GO:5215%2CGO,GO:6810%2CGO;function=ABC-type dipeptide/oligopeptide/nickel transport systems%2C permease components;locus_tag=ACN6KE_006666;note=Transmembrane subunit %28TM%29 found in Periplasmic Binding Protein %28PBP%29-dependent ATP-Binding Cassette %28ABC%29 transporters which generally bind type 2 PBPs. These types of transporters consist of a PBP%2C two TMs%2C and two cytoplasmic ABC ATPase subunits%2C and are mainly involved in importing solutes from the environment. The solute is captured by the PBP which delivers it to a gated translocation pathway formed by the two TMs. The two ABCs bind and hydrolyze ATP and drive the transport reaction. For these transporters the ABCs and TMs are on independent polypeptide chains. These systems transport a diverse range of substrates. Most are specific for a single substrate or a group of related substrates%3B however some transporters are more promiscuous%2C transporting structurally diverse substrates such as the histidine/lysine and arginine transporter in Enterobacteriaceae. In the latter case%2C this is achieved through binding different PBPs with different specificities to the TMs. For other promiscuous transporters such as the multiple-sugar transporter Msm of Streptococcus mutans%2C the PBP has a wide substrate specificity. These transporters include the maltose-maltodextrin%2C phosphate and sulfate transporters%2C among others.%2CFamily membership;product=putative peptide ABC transporter permease protein y4tP;protein_id=ACN6KE:HE616899.1644;transl_table=11;
